From 4ba08ba1936bcbeab9591380bcfb451925abe9e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: titanism <101466223+titanism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:34:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(billing): stop storing one Stripe payment intent twice

The unique sparse indexes on stripe_payment_intent_id, paypal_order_id
and paypal_transaction_id were never built: each field also had
`index: true`, which created a plain index under the same name first, so
the unique one failed. Concurrent webhooks and the sync job then stored
some payments twice, which added an extra period to the plan expiry and
made every later sync fail with "too many payments".

models:
- drop `index: true` from the three fields so the unique indexes build
- tag the pre-save duplicate error with code PAYMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS

billing:
- treat PAYMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS as a concurrent duplicate in the Stripe
  sync, the Stripe redirect and the PayPal handlers (the old message
  check never matched the translated message)
- Stripe redirect rethrows when the existing payment can't be found

scripts:
- remove-duplicate-payments: keep one payment per payment intent (the
  refunded one, otherwise the oldest), back up and delete the rest,
  sync it from Stripe again, build the unique indexes and save the
  affected users again
